            "heading": "Figure 1",
            "source_image_paths": [
              "2605.06667v1/teaser6.png"
            ],
            "source_caption": "Figure 1. Overview. ActCam enables zero-shot joint control of acting motion and camera motion for single-image video generation from a reference image, assuming only widespread conditioning capability of the backbone model on depth and keypoints. Given a reference image, an acting video representing the desired motion, and a target per-frame camera trajectory, ActCam generates a video that preserves identity while following both motion and cinematography.",
            "assigned_assets": [
              {
                "path": "/home/dictation/paper-fetch-skill/.paper-fetch-runs/official-reacquisition-2026-09-19/papers/2605.06667v1_assets/pipeline.png",
                "download_url": "https://arxiv.org/e-print/2605.06667v1#figures/pipeline.pdf",
                "caption": "Figure 1. Overview. ActCam enables zero-shot joint control of acting motion and camera motion for single-image video generation from a reference image, assuming only widespread conditioning capability of the backbone model on depth and keypoints. Given a reference image, an acting video representing the desired motion, and a target per-frame camera trajectory, ActCam generates a video that preserves identity while following both motion and cinematography.",
                "sha256": "8e9dcad89cd7b95f931b943c37ab3c99060992ba432b5f10f9a47985e3d108ab",
                "output_lines": [
                  28,
